325 proposals for the eu of tomorrow  have been adopted in an unprecedented  exercise in european democracy  the proposals from the final plenary  meeting of the conference on the future  of europe are based on the priorities  and recommendations of european citizens  ideas were submitted online debated at  grassroots events in citizens panels of  the parliament in strasbourg and across  europe and in conference  plenaries there is in fact no opposition  between or no contradiction between  representative democracy and  participatory democracy i don't believe  anymore in a democracy that is only  an election every five years without  involvement of the citizens  this weekend participants of the  conference plenary met in strasbourg to  adopt 325 proposals across nine themes  ranging from health to the economy  migration to climate change  there is a huge consensus in the main  pillars of the conclusions and that we  are really resoluted to  put forward and to implement your  recommendations that by the way after  this dialogue are also our  recommendations  some of the more ambitious proposals  like ending country's veto powers in the  council would require treaty changes  a broad majority of parliament's  delegation supported the proposals but  consensus did not mean unanimity  it is difficult for the ecr group to  endorse these recommendations  and it should be clear that the position  of the european parliament is not  unanimous  citizens were at the heart of the  process determined to ensure their  voices would be heard  what will happen next how will these  draft recommendations  that we have  adopted this morning how will they be  taken forward they cannot be allowed  gather dust in some report on a shell  the final report will be presented to  the presidents of the eu institutions at  the closing ceremony in strasbourg on  europe day on the 9th of may  [Music]
 

